    "name": "count-max-the-week-that-begins-in-the-published-month",
    "why": "The first window-located seam case. A department's week does not stop at the 1st: the week holding 1 August began on 26 July, in a month somebody else already published, and a cap measured only over the horizon reports one duty where the person has three. p-ali took the 30th and the 31st in the carry-in tail and the 1st in the draft, against a cap of two — so the violation is located at a window beginning six days before the horizon and is emitted because a WINDOW need only TOUCH what is being evaluated, where the containment reading would delete it silently. Take the history away and the same call must go quiet and say why, which is what the seam guard asserts.",
